  "strategy": "## 1. Approach and Rationale  \nThe problem requires finding a step function h: [0,2] \u21a6 [0,1] with integral 1 that minimizes the maximum overlap integral C_5. The existing approach uses constrained optimization with alternating LP and SLSQP phases, which improves incrementally but may get stuck in local optima. The key bottleneck is the reliance on gradient-based local search, which is limited by the initial solution.  \n\nWe propose a multi-resolution strategy to escape local optima by:  \n- Using a relatively simple construction (initial_h_values) as the base solution  \n- Refining it through:  \n  - Global sampling with controlled random perturbations  \n  - Local optimizations using linear constraints \n  - Resolution adjustment (using interpolation)  \nThe goal is to explore diverse topologies without relying heavily on sensitive gradient information.  \n\n## 2. Mathematical Specification  \nLet h \u2208 R^{n_points} be the function samples with:  \n- h[i] \u2208 [0, 1] for all i  \n- sum(h) = n_points/2  \n- n_points = number of points (400 in initial solution)  \n\nObjective: Minimize C_5 = max_k (dx * correlation(h, 1-h)[k])  \nwhere dx = 2/n_points, and correlation is computed with mode='full'.  \n\nThe optimization proceeds with:  \n- Feasible space: h masked so that 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and sum(h) = n_points/2  \n- Objective decreases when the maximum lag-wise overlap integral is reduced  \n\n## 3. Implementation Procedure  \n### Initial Setup  \nRead initial_h_values (seed=42, 400 points). Target sum = 200.  \n\n### Core Procedure (Phase 1-9)  \nWhile time remains:  \n1. **Sampling & Projection**:  \n   - Perturb 1-4 random indices by \u00b10.01 (minor perturbation)  \n   - Clip values to [0,1]  \n   - Adjust sum to 200 if necessary (projection)  \n   - Skip run if sum too close (threshold 1e-10)  \n\n2. **Local Optimization**:  \n   - For lag ranges (-offset to offset+), formulate LP: min max_lag {sum_i h[i]*(1-h[i+k])dx} over h[i] in [0,1] with sum fixed  \n   - Use CVXOPT sparse solver with weighted constraints  \n   - Update solution at each lag in a sliding window  \n\n3. **Resolution Adjustment**:  \n   - Check if solution is dominated:  \n     - If n_points < 300: interpolate to 400 points  \n     - If n_points > 400: decimate to 400 points  \n   - Only proceed if interpolated solution is feasible  \n\n4. **Termination**:  \n   - Complete 11-20 iterations (average over 600s)  \n   - Track best solution globally  \n   - If any phase stalled (no improvement \u22651e-4 for 100 iterations), restart  \n\n### Helper Functions  \n- `project_feasible(h, target)`: Clips and adjusts sum to target  \n- `compute_c5(h)`: Returns C_5 with feasibility check  \n- `interpolate_to()`: Spline interpolation between representatives  \n\n## 4. Search Choices and Variations  \n**Key Heuristics**:  \n- **Perturbation energy**: 0.001-0.01% of max value  \n- **Resolution range**: 200-800 points (original: 400)  \n- **Stall tolerance**: 1e-5 of best score  \n\n**Pivotal Decisions**:  \n1. If sum out-of-bound (exceeding 1e-10): Adjust only if absolute error > 1e-8  \n2. Skip constraint for almost-saturated values (h[i] < 1e-6 or > 1-1e-6)  \n3. If all LP solutions similar to initial:  \n   - Randomly reset top 10% of samples (target sum maintained)  \n\n**Failover Options**:  \n- Dual annealing (if reduced gradient unavailable)  \n- Alternative initial sample (random pulse pattern)  \n\n## 5. Budget and Robustness  \nDominant cost: 200-300s for 400-point evaluation (1600 operations)  \n- Cost estimation per phase unit: 10-20 evaluations  \n- Early termination if progress stalls  \n\nImplementation guardrails:  \n- `n_trials = min(20, budget_s/60)`  \n- Time check at start of each evaluation  \n- Exception: restart if time > 85% budget_s  \n\n## 6. Validation and Return Contract  \nFinal output: (h_final, c5_final, best_n_points)  \n\n- Check n_points \u2208 [200, 800]  \n- Verify sum(h) \u2248 200 \u00b1 1e-5  \n- Repeat objective calculation for best solution  \n- Minimum acceptable improvement: 1e-7 relative to parent  \n\nFallback procedure if emergency halt: Return nearest feasible solution from parent",
